## Remaining WARN explanation (local glossary only)

Local-glossary WARNs are **约定译法 phrasing mismatches**, not missing concepts. The book consistently uses readable forms established from early blocks; the local glossary entries include parenthetical/alternate phrasings that the checker treats as required strings:

| Glossary entry (checker expects) | Book convention used | Reason |
|---|---|---|
| `演化而来的` | `进化而来的` | Matches prior chapters & style_psychology readability; titles also use 进化 |
| `"天生如此"的故事` | `恰好如此故事` | Body convention from Ch.1–3; title uses 天生如此 but narrative uses 恰好如此 |
| `适应（物）` | `适应` | Parenthetical glossary note; body uses 适应 |
| `实然—应然（问题）` | `实然—应然鸿沟` / `实然`/`应然` | Full phrase with 问题 is glossary annotation; body uses 鸿沟 |
| `WEIRD（西方、受教育、工业化、富裕、民主）` | `WEIRD` after first expanded mention | First-mention expansion present where introduced; later uses bare WEIRD |
| `副产物` (title) vs body | `副产品` in body | Body convention from Ch.2–3 definitions; title uses 副产物 |

These are **not** ERROR-level issues. Shared-glossary verify is clean. Changing either glossary was forbidden (shared/local glossaries not to be edited by translation agents).

